No, killing your pet does not normally anger your god.  The exception
is that if you displace it into a trap or water, and it dies as a
result, you will usually "feel guilty about losing your pet like this"
meaning that your god is angry.

> The "rumble of distant thunder" is what happens when you kill your
> pet. You lose a large number (15?) of ALIGNMENT points - it counts as
> a major sin. 

This is true, and you also lose 1 point of luck.

> Naturally, this is usually enough to take your alignment
> into negative territory (you have "strayed", "sinned" or even
> "transgressed"). 

This, however, is only true early in the game.  Later on, your
alignment will be so high (as a result of killing many many hostile
monsters) that you can take the 15 point penalty and still be piously
aligned.  FYI, you can check your alignment with a stethoscope or a
potion or wand of enlightenment.




